<section>
	<h2 id="translations">Translations</h2>
	<p>
		The theme's own text, such as the pattern copy, block style names and the 404 page, comes translated into Czech, Danish, Dutch, French, German, Italian, Polish, Portuguese, Russian, Slovenian, Spanish, Swedish and Turkish. WordPress uses the translation that matches the language in <strong>Settings &gt; General &gt; Site Language</strong>.
	</p>
	<p>
		A pattern is translated when you insert it, into the language of your WordPress dashboard, so set the language before you build your pages. Your header and footer follow the site language until you edit them. The demo content stays in English, because its pages, menu and booking form come from the demo site.
	</p>
	<p>
		To change a translation or add another language, use a plugin such as <a href="https://wordpress.org/plugins/loco-translate/" target="_blank">Loco Translate</a>. We have <a href="https://www.proteusthemes.com/help/translate-theme-another-language/">an article with a video on how to translate our themes</a>.
	</p>
</section>
